WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
It is a monthly payment for people on a low income, whether or not they work. In general you must: be 18 or over (there are exceptions at 16 or 17) and be under State Pension age.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:28.200
Have £16,000 or less in money, savings and investments. Live in the United Kingdom. If you are from the EU, you may need settled or pre-settled status.

3
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:44.200
Many visas carry the condition «no recourse to public funds» (NRPF). If your visa has it, you CANNOT claim Universal Credit, Housing Benefit or Council Tax Reduction, among others. Claiming anyway can cause problems with your immigration status and force you to pay the money back.

4
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:56.000
Some contribution-based benefits (such as New Style JSA or Statutory Sick Pay) do not count as public funds. If in doubt, get advice before you apply.

5
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.200
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
